            <ArticleTitle>Primary omental pregnancy presenting with hemorrhagic shock. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>116-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Abdominal pregnancy is a very rare and serious type of extrauterine gestation that accounts for approximately 0.003% of all ectopic pregnancies. Omental pregnancy, an extremely rare form of abdominal pregnancy, can be primary or secondary to a tubal pregnancy that aborts out of the fimbria and reimplants in the peritoneal cavity. We present an additional case of primary omental pregnancy at 12 gestational weeks presenting with symptoms of hemoperitoneum and acute abdomen.</AbstractText>
